Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their possible usage
• `event_date`        : filter to December 2020 (`LIKE '202012%'` or `_TABLE_SUFFIX BETWEEN '01' AND '31'`)  
• `event_name`        : pick only the beginning of each session (`= 'session_start'`)  
• `event_params`      : UNNEST to pull the parameters that identify a session and its acquisition info  
      – key = 'ga_session_id'   → the session ID (INT64)  
      – key = 'source'          → campaign source (STRING)  
      – key = 'medium'          → campaign medium (STRING)  
• `user_pseudo_id`    : together with `ga_session_id`, forms a unique session key  
• `traffic_source`    : backup source / medium fields (`traffic_source.source` and `traffic_source.medium`)  
Conditions that may be used
• `_TABLE_SUFFIX` LIKE '202012%'  or wildcard table `events_202012*`  
• `event_name = 'session_start'`  
• `key IN ('ga_session_id','source','medium')` when filtering inside `UNNEST(event_params)`  

Below are ten exploratory‑to‑final BigQuery queries (all capped with LIMIT 20) that gradually dig into the data and end with the required result.  
(Remember to run them one‑by‑one – they are meant for learning the data step‑by‑step.)

```sql
-- Description: 1) Quick look at December‑01 events
SELECT
  event_date,
  event_name,
  user_pseudo_id,
  event_params
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_20201201`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: 2) List the different parameter keys that exist on 1 Dec 2020
SELECT DISTINCT ep.key
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_20201201`,
UNNEST(event_params) AS ep
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: 3) Pull parameter values of interest (source, medium, ga_session_id) for a few rows
SELECT
  user_pseudo_id,
  MAX(CASE WHEN ep.key = 'ga_session_id' THEN CAST(ep.value.int_value AS INT64) END)     AS ga_session_id,
  MAX(CASE WHEN ep.key = 'source'        THEN ep.value.string_value END)                 AS source,
  MAX(CASE WHEN ep.key = 'medium'        THEN ep.value.string_value END)                 AS medium
FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_20201201`,
UNNEST(event_params) AS ep
WHERE event_name = 'session_start'
GROUP BY user_pseudo_id
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: 4) Distinct source / medium combinations on 1 Dec 2020
SELECT DISTINCT
  src_med.source,
  src_med.medium
FROM (
  SELECT
    MAX(CASE WHEN ep.key = 'source' THEN ep.value.string_value END)  AS source,
    MAX(CASE WHEN ep.key = 'medium' THEN ep.value.string_value END)  AS medium
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_20201201`,
  UNNEST(event_params) AS ep
  WHERE event_name = 'session_start'
  GROUP BY user_pseudo_id
) AS src_med
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: 5) Count distinct sessions (user_pseudo_id + ga_session_id) for 1 Dec
SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT CONCAT(user_pseudo_id,'_',CAST(ga_session_id AS STRING))) AS sessions_1dec
FROM (
  SELECT
    user_pseudo_id,
    MAX(CASE WHEN ep.key = 'ga_session_id' THEN CAST(ep.value.int_value AS INT64) END) AS ga_session_id
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.ga4_obfuscated_sample_ecommerce.events_20201201`,
  UNNEST(event_params) AS ep
  WHERE event_name = 'session_start'
  GROUP BY user_pseudo_id
)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
